  "id": "COMPOUND:32773 - PROTEIN:6324",
  "verbalization": "Lup-20(29)-en-3-ol, (3beta)- is consistently identified as a target of multiple compounds, all of which ultimately lead to the M-phase phosphoprotein 8. This suggests a shared mechanism of action involving the protein M-phase phosphoprotein 8, which is involved in the cell cycle and mitosis. The evidence indicates that Lup-20(29)-en-3-ol, (3beta)- acts as a modulator of the target protein through a series of intermediate compounds, each of which is a known inhibitor of M-phase phosphoprotein 8. The presence of multiple distinct compounds targeting the same protein suggests that the relationship is not direct but rather involves a complex regulatory pathway. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Lup-20(29)-en-3-ol, (3beta)- may influence M-phase phosphoprotein 8 through a network of interacting molecules, potentially affecting the cell cycle's progression.",
